# desktop tile on: windows side by side, as on Omarchy (Hyprland's dwindle).
# Below the button row (30 pixels) with gaps of 8: one window takes it all
# (236x62 characters at 1920x1080); a second one takes the right half, and
# the console's window the left (117 columns); when it goes, all again.
@disk
@usb kbd mouse
$ layout us
$ desktop tile on
windows are tiled: side by side, the newest splitting the space of the one before (saved)
$ desktop
~ the terminal window has 236x62 characters
~ windows are tiled
$ monitor
the system monitor in a new window: q leaves
$ sleep 1
$ desktop
~ the terminal window has 117x62 characters
# The monitor's title bar at the right, focused (blue).
@screenshot 1920x1080 pixels 970,42=3a6ea5 20,42=8a9bb0
@keys q
$ sleep 1
$ desktop
~ the terminal window has 236x62 characters
# Saved: after a restart the windows are tiled again.
@reboot
$ desktop
~ windows are tiled
$ desktop tile off
windows float again: drag them by the title bar, resize them by the grip (saved)
